==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Nuclear Blade Dragon King Berius''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Nuclear Dragon King Berius is good in [[Into the Future]], with a decent health pool and all around nice stats for that point in the game, though his [[Knockback]] isn't guaranteed. He's also slow and has few knockbacks, though he functions more as a crowd-control midrange tank rather than a pureblooded ranger. Assuming you don't push ridiculously hard into any dangerous backliners present, Berius' Knockback should be a fine addition to your defense.

With the introduction of [[Cats of the Cosmos]] and more advanced Alien enemies, however, another issue rears its head: a lack of [[Immune to Warp|Warp Immunity]]. On one hand, this allows Berius to reposition as his knockback count is low. On the other hand, he can't properly utilize his tanky properties—[[Corporal Weyland]], [[Gardeneel Bros.]], and [[Ribbo]] can snipe him and put him in unfavorable positions, and [[Star Peng]] flicks him away like nothing. A lack of [[Barrier Breaker]] can be annoying also, since [[Barrier]]s prevent crowd-control abilities from being applied. The [[Nature's Guardians ELEMENTAL PIXIES (Gacha Event)|ELEMENTAL PIXIES]] have none of these issues while doing one or more of Berius' jobs better (and being severely cheaper at that), thus making him quite underwhelming.

Assuming lategame is a factor in the PC version, he is severely outdated for that. His DPS, although great for its time, is quite subpar compared to the generalists of today, like [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]], her [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|uncanny counterpart]], and other gacha options. His lack of any valuable immunities also means his already subpar crowd-control will likely not work due to his weakness to enemies like [[Loris]].

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller & Backliner}}

